From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-embed-feedstock <noreply@github.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Write pch cflags as a list, not a map object

Backport of nodejs/gyp-next#355 (merged 2026-08-27, not in any release;
node 26.6.0 vendors gyp-next 0.22.2).

On Windows, gyp's ninja generator hands the precompiled-header compile a
Python `map` iterator where it means a list of flags, and ninja_syntax
writes its repr into build.ninja:

  cflags_cc = <map object at 0x000002791210AB30>

The three targets that use a pch (v8_base_without_compiler, v8_compiler,
v8_initializers) therefore compile their pch source with NO C++ flags --
no /std:c++20, no /Zc:__cplusplus, nothing -- and cl.exe reports the
repr's tokens as "unrecognized source file type '<map'".  Node never
sees it: its Windows builds go through MSBuild, not ninja, and the ninja
path is nodejs/node#57633, closed as stale.

Only the pch compile step is affected; every other object gets its flags
from the target-level variable, which is a list.
---
 tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/msvs_emulation.py | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/msvs_emulation.py b/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/msvs_emulation.py
--- a/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/msvs_emulation.py
+++ b/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/msvs_emulation.py
@@ -1057,13 +1057,18 @@ def GetFlagsModifications(
             pch_output = ["/Yc" + self._PchHeader()]
             if command == "cxx":
                 return (
-                    [("cflags_cc", map(expand_special, cflags_cc + pch_output))],
+                    [
+                        (
+                            "cflags_cc",
+                            [expand_special(x) for x in cflags_cc + pch_output],
+                        )
+                    ],
                     self.output_obj,
                     [],
                 )
             elif command == "cc":
                 return (
-                    [("cflags_c", map(expand_special, cflags_c + pch_output))],
+                    [("cflags_c", [expand_special(x) for x in cflags_c + pch_output])],
                     self.output_obj,
                     [],
                 )
